# Line-ending policy for a hash-bound corpus.
#
# The determinism gates compare bytes and hash source files, so a checkout that
# rewrites line endings makes them fail. With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes,
# a fresh Windows checkout receives CRLF while the index stores LF, and
# build_hlr_import_bundle.py --check and build_trace_graph.py --check both report
# drift that does not exist. Normalizing to LF in the working tree keeps the
# controlled artifacts byte-identical on every platform.
#
# The gates deliberately stay byte-exact. Relaxing them to ignore line endings
# would weaken a determinism control to work around a checkout setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never filtered, never diffed as text.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.zip   binary

# MPS persistence is XML that MPS writes and reviewers read. It is text, kept at LF
# by the rule above so file-per-root diffs stay reviewable and deterministic.
# ADR-001 prohibits hand-editing it; that is a process control, not a reason to
# make it opaque to review.
